+      "title": "The recorded derivative inequality does not imply susceptibility divergence",
+      "statement": "The implications theta(delta)~delta and theta'(delta)<=C*chi(delta), even with theta,chi positive and smooth on 0<delta<1, do not imply chi(delta)>=c/delta for any c>0. Therefore the earlier C0065 attempt's claimed inverse-distance lower bound does not follow from the two displayed premises. This refutes that inference, not the percolation lower bound itself. Scope: No claim is made that the actual high-dimensional finite-cluster susceptibility has this counterexample behavior. The claimed percolation theorem must be re-proved from valid percolation-specific inputs.",
